@namespace SpaceSails.Client.Pages
@implements IHandleEvent
@using System.Globalization
@using SpaceSails.Client.Rendering
@using SpaceSails.Contracts
@using SpaceSails.Core
@using SpaceSails.Core.Interior
@*
    #251 item 1 · THE PAPER ON THE TABLE, ON ITS OWN FILE.

    Moved out of Map.razor by PURE MOTION — the block between the two fences below is the block that was in
    the page, character for character. Every page member it reads is a [Parameter] with the SAME NAME (the
    fields keep their underscore, the methods come across as delegates), which is what lets the markup move
    without a rewrite and lets the suite's source guards read it through MapMarkup exactly as before.

    The `@if` that opens it stays in Map.razor: the page keeps its paint order in one place, and a closed
    surface still renders nothing. IHandleEvent repeats the page's own override (Map.Sim.cs) — without it
    Blazor would put an automatic re-render back on every event in here, which the page turns off because
    the HUD's refresh belongs to OnTick's 200 ms throttle. The .razor.css beside this file carries no rules;
    it exists to give the component Map.razor.css's scope (#251 item 3 moves the rules).

    The `@{ }` around the fences is not decoration: the block used to sit inside `@if (…) { … }`,
    which is a Razor CODE block, and a code block is where its first statements are legal. The braces
    put the moved lines back in the context they were written in; they are outside the fences, so what
    the source guards read is still exactly the lines that were in the page.
*@
@* ── THE PAGE'S OWN NOTE ON THIS SURFACE, moved here with it (#251 item 1) and not touched by a
   word: it is the paragraph that stood above this block in Map.razor. It sits ABOVE the fence, not
   inside it, so that a source guard slicing the block by text goes on reading markup and not prose.
   ── *@
    @* ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
       #1052 (L2) · THE PAPER AT THE TABLE — AND IT IS DOCKED, NOT MODAL.

       Owner, 2026-09-01, and this block is the sentence answered literally: "Just hope there is a way to
       have both the newsfeed and pop-up-bar walkers visible UI at the same time."

       SO THERE IS NO .view-object-backdrop IN HERE AT ALL — no scrim, no blur, no centring, and the guard
       asserts the ABSENCE rather than trusting this comment. That is #784's own move made a second time: a
       strip at the foot for the sitting, a panel at the side for the paper, and between them a hall that is
       still lit, still walked, and still clickable. A rep who crosses the floor while the captain is reading
       raises his card at 1320 and lands ON TOP of this panel, which is the right way round: the man talking
       to you outranks the paper in your hands. The panel does not move and does not close, so putting his
       card down leaves the captain reading where he was.

       IT LIVES OUTSIDE THE SEATED REGION AND IS GATED ON THE SEAT ANYWAY. Standing up takes the paper with
       it (there is nowhere to read it from), and the panel is not inside `.seated-dock` because the strip is
       a short pinned row at the foot of the glass and a paper folded into it would grow the strip into the
       modal it stopped being.

       CappedScrollPanel is inside NewsWirePanel, so the head — the masthead and today's story — keeps its
       measured height and only the dated list gives. Elegant minimalism: the scroll bar arrives when the
       list is longer than the panel and not before.
       ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ *@

@{
@* ── MARKUP BEGINS · verbatim from Map.razor ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── *@
        <div class="seated-news">
            @* The shell's Bare frame and the .view-object family's own foot, exactly as the galley card
               wears them — this is the same wire in a different box, and the box is the only new thing. *@
            <OverlayShell class="view-object seated-news-card text-light" StopClicks="true"
                          Frame="OverlayFrame.Bare" Dismiss="OverlayDismiss.Close"
                          DismissClass="view-object-close" DismissFace="Close"
                          DismissLabel="Put the paper down"
                          DismissTitle="Put the paper down — Esc does the same"
                          OnClose="() => Dismiss(CloseSeatedNews)">
                @* THE ✂ ON EVERY ROW, handed to the wire component rather than written beside it, so the
                   headline row and the dated rows below it cannot come to offer different controls.

                   READING FILES NOTHING. The scissors is the only thing on this panel that touches the
                   book, and it is a press — #602's ammo-as-evidence, one system over: what is in the book
                   got there because a hand put it there. The row says where the paper is once it is in
                   (SeatedSpread.ClippedLabel) rather than going dead, which is #212/#603's rule. *@
                <SpaceSails.Client.Pages.Stations.NewsWirePanel
                    SimTime="SimTime" Feed="SeatedNewsFeed()" ItemCount="SeatedNewsItemCount">
                    <RowAction Context="story">
                        <button type="button" class="news-clip"
                                title="@SpaceSails.Core.SeatedSpread.ClipHint"
                                @onclick="() => ClipThisStory(story)">@(AlreadyClipped(story)
                                    ? SpaceSails.Core.SeatedSpread.ClippedLabel
                                    : SpaceSails.Core.SeatedSpread.ClipLabel)</button>
                    </RowAction>
                </SpaceSails.Client.Pages.Stations.NewsWirePanel>
            </OverlayShell>
        </div>
@* ── MARKUP ENDS ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── *@
}

@code {
    // ── WHAT THESE PARAMETERS ARE ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
    //
    // #251 item 1 · Every [Parameter] below carries a member of the page under THE MEMBER'S OWN NAME —
    // a field keeps its underscore, a method arrives as a delegate with its own signature, a variable the
    // page's `@if` binds arrives under the name the `@if` gave it. That is the whole trick of this
    // refactor: it is what let the markup above move out of Map.razor without a single character of it
    // changing, and what lets the suite's source guards read it through MapMarkup exactly as they read it
    // when it lived in the page. A parameter that needs saying more than that says it on its own line.

    [Parameter] public Func<NewsWire.NewsItem, bool> AlreadyClipped { get; set; } = default!;
    [Parameter] public Action<NewsWire.NewsItem> ClipThisStory { get; set; } = default!;
    [Parameter] public Action CloseSeatedNews { get; set; } = default!;
    [Parameter] public Func<Action, Task> Dismiss { get; set; } = default!;
    [Parameter] public Func<IReadOnlyList<NewsWire.NewsItem>> SeatedNewsFeed { get; set; } = default!;
    [Parameter] public int SeatedNewsItemCount { get; set; }
    [Parameter] public double SimTime { get; set; }

    // The page's own event dispatch, repeated: no automatic re-render per event.
    Task IHandleEvent.HandleEventAsync(EventCallbackWorkItem callback, object? arg) => callback.InvokeAsync(arg);
}
